 Beerockxs, neutral femal priestess

This was a pretty straightforward game, although it's only my second
ascension. I found +4 speed boots on dlvl2, a magic lamp in the mines
above minetown gave me GDSM, and some saccing on the Minetown Altar gave
Mojo.
Nothing really special afterwards, Soko gave a "oR, and after I looted
Ludious (where I got TC due to a Tengu and Teleportitis due to a
leprechaun) I used another magic lamp I found on the quest to get a BoH,
never found another one for the entire game. The quest was pretty easy,
the Zombie hordes made me feel like I was starring in Dawn of the Dead
or something :-).
After the quest I looted the Castle pretty easily, this time I lowered
the drawbridge. I use the castle wand to get 2 magic markers to enchant
my stuff, and used 3 or 4 wishes to finally get the PYEC. Before
Gehemnon I sacced for a pretty long time to get Magicbane, that's why I
had so many weapon artifacts. Gehemnon was pretty easy with  Magic
Mapping at just 15% fail.
During that time I lost my protection twice, due to saccing of a
Lieutenant and a Doppelganger. There were enough priests around to get
around that, so I just killed the one I had donated to earlier and took
my zorkmids to another one, that also got me back my robe I had lost
earlier when stepping onto a polytrap.
Vlad died like the wimp he is, but I killed Rodney above water when
trying to get the book and of course I had no /oCold to get it out, so I
had to track back to my stash in Ludious at dlvl19 to get one.
In the sanctum I got a wee bit worried when my hitpoints dropped below
100 for the first time in the game when I was surrounded by 4 priests of
Moloch, but just on !oFH gave me enough time to finish them with some
magic missiles.
On the way back up, Rodney showed up only once, and the mysterious force
was bearable.
Planes were pretty easy too, confused ?oGD works just fine, and on Fire,
the portal was just 3 steps away.
 I just had to spend some time on the plane of water, killing lots of
sharks, kraken, and jellyfish.
On Astral, I decided to go left, because I didn't want to face Death who
has on the right side. After some whacking and magic missiling and
/oDeathing, I was at the right altar. :-)

